---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { listReleases } from '../lib/releases';
const releases = listReleases();
const latest = releases[0];
const tiers = [
  ['under 10', 'Nothing under the compound\'s name. Counted inside its mechanism class.'],
  ['10', 'Report count. Route and source channel, as counts.'],
  ['50', 'What people took it for, dose ranges, frequency, duration, purity testing, handling, adverse effects, status — as counts.'],
  ['100', 'Outcome by goal: of the people who took it hoping for X, how many reported no change / slight / moderate / large.'],
  ['200', 'Percentages with intervals on everything above. When each effect started and whether it resolved.'],
  ['1,000', 'The one cross-compound view: outcome by goal, side by side, stratified, never pooled or ranked.'],
];
---
<Base title="Data">
  <h1>What is published</h1>
  {latest
    ? <p class="lede">The latest release is <a href={`/releases/${latest.dir}`}>{latest.release}</a>, computed on {latest.date} from {latest.counts.committed.toLocaleString('en-US')} committed reports. What appears in it, and when, is fixed by the <a href="/docs/release-spec">release specification</a> — not by what the data turns out to say.</p>
    : <p class="lede">Nothing yet. There have been no releases. What appears here, and when, is fixed by the <a href="/docs/release-spec">release specification</a> — not by what the data turns out to say.</p>}

  <p class="muted">No count is shown between releases. Each release publishes the number of reports as of that date, with the Merkle root of the submission log, so the number is checkable and never a live signal of when someone submitted.</p>

  <h2>How a compound earns its way onto this page</h2>
  <p>More is published about a compound as more people report on it, so that the number of published figures never gets close to the number of people they are computed from. A compound with 23 reports shows a count and two distributions. A compound with 300 shows everything.</p>
  <div class="ladder">
    {tiers.map(([at, what], i) => (
      <div class:list={['rung', { locked: true }]}>
        <span class="n">{i === 0 ? at : `${at}+ reports`}</span>
        <span>{what}</span>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p>Every figure carries its denominator and, once percentages appear, a 95% interval — inside the image, so a screenshot cannot lose them. Cells with fewer than 5 reports are shown as "fewer than 5." Nothing is ever ranked. See <a href="/docs/analyses-we-will-never-run">analyses we will never run</a>.</p>

  <h2>Releases</h2>
  {releases.length === 0
    ? <p class="muted">None yet. Each release will be listed here with its date, its signed tag, its transparency-log entry, and the Merkle root of the submission log at that moment.</p>
    : <div class="release-list">
        {releases.map((r) => <a href={`/releases/${r.dir}`}><span class="n">{r.release}</span><span>{r.date} · {r.counts.committed.toLocaleString('en-US')} committed · {r.counts.analyzed.toLocaleString('en-US')} analysed · root <code>{r.merkle.root.slice(0, 16)}…</code></span></a>)}
      </div>}
  <p class="muted">Every release can be checked without trusting us: <a href="/docs/how-to-verify">how to verify a release</a>.</p>
</Base>
